---
title: Jaunty.FlatFiles — CRUD & Write-Back Lifecycle
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ViewMode: FlatFileDatabase.Open()

    state ViewMode {
        [*] --> ViewCreated: CREATE VIEW FROM read_csv_auto()
        ViewCreated --> ReadOnly: Query via VIEW
        ReadOnly --> ReadOnly: .Where() .OrderBy() .Take()
    }

    ViewMode --> TableMode: First mutation (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)

    state TableMode {
        [*] --> Promoted: DROP VIEW + CREATE TABLE AS
        Promoted --> Modified: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE
        Modified --> Modified: More mutations
        Modified --> QueryModified: .Query() reads modified data
        QueryModified --> Modified
    }

    state WriteBack {
        [*] --> ChooseMode
        ChooseMode --> NonDestructive: SaveAsync("new-file.csv")
        ChooseMode --> Destructive: SaveAsync(WriteBackMode.Overwrite)
        ChooseMode --> CrossFormat: ExportAsync("output.parquet")

        NonDestructive --> CopyTo: COPY TO 'new-file.csv'
        Destructive --> TempFile: COPY TO 'temp-xyz.csv'
        TempFile --> AtomicRename: Rename temp → original
        CrossFormat --> CopyTo: COPY TO 'output.parquet' (FORMAT PARQUET)
    }

    TableMode --> WriteBack: SaveAsync() / ExportAsync()
    WriteBack --> [*]: File written to disk

    ViewMode --> Disposed: Dispose()
    TableMode --> Disposed: Dispose()
    Disposed --> [*]: DuckDB closed, handles released

    note right of ViewMode
        Lazy mode: data read from disk on query.
        Efficient for one-shot queries.
    end note

    note right of TableMode
        Eager mode: data in DuckDB columnar storage.
        Required for mutations.
        Automatic promotion — transparent to user.
    end note
